    "title": "Network service scan",
    "desc": "A program ran a port or service scanner - nmap, masscan, zmap, rustscan, naabu, unicornscan - or used netcat in zero-I/O scan mode (nc -z). Sweeping a host or network for open ports is the reconnaissance an attacker does to find what to pivot to (MITRE T1046); it is rarely something an application does in the course of its own work, so on a server or an agent account it is a clean signal. The bash /dev/tcp sweep form is also caught by reverse_shell's /dev/tcp branch.",
